{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And I said: Wisdom is better than strength.</b> Even though the wisdom of the poor man is despised and his words are not heeded, therefore in a time of need wisdom accomplishes what the mighty cannot accomplish. And the word וחכמה is deficient [without] אם, as if it said: \"and if the wisdom of the poor man is despised\" — like <i>וצמית והלכת אל הכלים</i>, meaning \"and if you set\" — and many like these exist."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The citation וצמית והלכת אל הכלים is not a standard verse; possibly corrupt or a paraphrased allusion. Rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:44.865100645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}